{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The grinding and cutting supplies fit the metalworking work suggested by my recent cutting wheels, drill bits, rivets, and measuring tools, provided the wheel size fits my equipment.",
    "The repair tape and countersunk screw assortment fit my repeated purchases of adhesives and fasteners for joining, mounting, and repairing materials."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shoe glue, clothing mailers, and cake drums solve needs I have not shown; buying workshop supplies does not mean I currently need every kind of repair or project supply.",
    "The plumbing couplings, long half-inch bolts, and aluminum profiles require particular connections or dimensions that my history does not establish.",
    "Printer filament assumes I own and use a compatible printer, and nothing in my recent purchases explains a need for rose-red material."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in DIY seems to have been stretched into an interest in supplies for almost any hands-on project.",
    "My frequent fastener purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to recommend hardware regardless of its size or intended use."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases repeatedly support practical fastening, metal cutting, measurement, and repair tasks; that continuity matters more than a broad connection to making things.",
    "Compatibility matters: the suggested four-and-a-half-inch wheels need checking against my equipment, and specific bolt lengths, fitting sizes, and profile dimensions need a matching job.",
    "I often buy useful assortments, but frequent purchasing does not mean I need a large quantity of an unrelated supply such as clothing mailers."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my workshop needs but stretched that interest into unrelated projects and supplies with unconfirmed compatibility."
}"}
